WEBVTT

00:00:00.682 --> 00:00:04.597
Tutorial four. Matching, regression and GEE.

00:00:10.954 --> 00:00:20.163
Propensity-score matching makes the groups comparable. Choose the covariates to match on. The method, the ratio and the caliper are all yours to set.

00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:27.676
A live preview runs the real matching on your settings. You see how many eyes each group keeps, before you commit to a run.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:36.065
The regression tab adds a covariate-adjusted model for every outcome. The adjusted effect is written beside the crude comparison.

00:00:36.332 --> 00:00:43.545
GEE models are clustered on the patient, so two eyes of one person are never counted as independent evidence.

00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:49.138
The GEE effect and its P value can be added as columns to the summary tables.

00:00:49.925 --> 00:00:54.398
StandardEyes. For ophthalmologists, by ophthalmologists.

